            "review_text": "Elise\nZhongshan District, Taipei109 contributions\n0\nComplete waist of money\nJun 2017 • Couples\nWe read some reviews before coming here. Some were good, some were bad but in general it seemed okay so we wanted to give it a shot.\n\nWe shouldn't have.\nI ordered pasta with tuna, thinking maybe it was fresh tuna. Nope. Straight out of a can with some oil on top of the pasta. Ta dah! Done! No sauce, no vegetables just plain pasta, canned tuna and oil (see picture). Yuck. My partner had noodles with vegetables and sea food which was acceptable. My dish turned out to be more expensive than his! 90.000 and his was 60.000! Outrageous!\n\nWe thought: okay maybe something sweet as dessert, pancakes with chocolate. I don't know what happened but it took forever while out main course arrived nearly immediately after we ordered. When we got the pancakes they were stacked on top of each other with just a little drizzle of chocolate. I went to ask for more chocolate sauce and they just didn't understand. When they finally did the told us it would cost us extra, so we didn't. \n\nJust.... don't eat here. Really. It's expensive, the food is gross and service is bad.\nRead more\nWritten June 1, 2017",
